OL,3,GNEWSALimb falls off dead 'Robin Hood'
OL,4,Aoak tree
OL,5,
OL,6,FA limb has fallen off one of the UK's
OL,7,Fmost iconic oak trees two months after
OL,8,Fexperts said it had died.
OL,10,FThe Major Oak is estimated to have
OL,11,Flived in Sherwood Forest in
OL,12,FNottinghamshire for up to 1,200 years,
OL,13,Fand has links to the legend of Robin
OL,14,FHood.
OL,16,FThe Royal Society for the Protection of
OL,17,FBirds (RSPB) - the conservation charity
OL,18,Fwhich manages the forest - said in
OL,19,FJune, after the tree's first spring
OL,20,Fwith no leaves, the Major Oak had died.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
